<div class="guide-introduction">
  <p>
    Roughly is an open collection of the world’s percentages. It brings together questions about people’s experiences, circumstances, actions, and preferences, along with the evidence available to answer them.
  </p>
  <p>
    To interpret a percentage, you need to know what it describes. This guide explains the language, the limits of the evidence, and the thinking behind the project.
  </p>
</div>
<div id="guide-start" class="guide-chapters">
  <.link navigate={~p"/guide/percentages"}>
    <span class="guide-chapter-number">01</span><div>
      <h2>What a percentage describes</h2><p>
        A condition, a population, a time, and a result. Follow one example from a question to a statistical statement.
      </p>
    </div><.icon name="hero-arrow-right" class="size-5" />
  </.link>
  <.link navigate={~p"/guide/knowledge"}>
    <span class="guide-chapter-number">02</span><div>
      <h2>What can we know?</h2><p>
        How a fact about human life differs from a recorded answer, and why subjective experiences can still be studied.
      </p>
    </div><.icon name="hero-arrow-right" class="size-5" />
  </.link>
  <.link navigate={~p"/guide/reading"}>
    <span class="guide-chapter-number">03</span><div>
      <h2>Ideas and sources</h2><p>
        Explore connections to philosophy, measurement, statistics, and collective intelligence.
      </p>
    </div><.icon name="hero-arrow-right" class="size-5" />
  </.link>
</div>
<h2 id="guide-open-work">An open body of work</h2>
<p>
  The software, definitions, and methods are open to contribution. The
  <a href="https://github.com/bcooke/roughly/tree/main/vault">project’s knowledge vault</a>
  contains the deeper research, proposals, and technical decisions behind these explanations.
</p>

<p>
  <a id="guide-contributing" href="https://github.com/bcooke/roughly/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">Read the contribution guide</a>
  for the available ways to help with the software and documentation.
</p>
